messages:
sylvia: heads up — seeing a weird provisioning loop on gpu-nodepool after the gitops apply. seems Helm helpers are rendering an empty map as a present nodeSelector which flips autoscaler behavior :/

dhruv: ugh. any repro steps or snippet?

sylvia: minimal repro: values.yaml has gpuPools: {} and our helper does default .Values.gpuPools to {} via coalesce. template ends up emitting: 
```yaml
nodeSelector: {}
```
K8s autoscaler + cluster-autoscaler logic reads that as a change and tries to reconcile, which triggers terraform/gke node reprovision in our infra flow.

ben: interesting — empty map vs null matters across tools. some patches treat {} as explicit override. coalesce makes it non-nil. you want to keep it nil/unset when user gives an empty object.

marco: can you paste the helper? iirc we use a helper that does `{{ default dict .Values.nodeSelector }}` which will create empty map if missing. that explains it.

sylvia: exact helper: 
```gotemplate
{{- define "common.nodeSelector" -}}
{{- $ns := coalesce .Values.nodeSelector (dict) -}}
{{- if not (empty $ns) -}}
nodeSelector: {{ toYaml $ns | nindent 2 }}
{{- end -}}
{{- end -}}
```
but in our usage we pass `.Values.gpuPools[.name].nodeSelector` where gpuPools entry can be present but intentionally empty in values.yaml (we use empty map to denote default behaviour). coalesce turns nil into {} earlier in the chart processing and later the `empty` check is fooled in some edge cases in helm v3 templating when types are coerced.

dhruv: hmm, helm's `empty` function considers `{}` empty I thought. is this Helm 3.12 subtlety?

ben: `empty` returns true for empty map/slice/string, yes. but coalesce returning a typed map vs nil sometimes interacts with Sprig helpers or `toYaml` causing `nodeSelector: {}` to be rendered (not caught by kustomize merge). Also CI linters (helm lint) can be silent.

marco: quick fix: avoid coalesce with dict() in the helper. Instead check if the value is set and only render when set and non-empty. e.g.: 
```gotemplate
{{- $v := index .Values "gpuPools" | default nil -}}
{{- $pool := index $v .name | default nil -}}
{{- if and $pool (not (empty $pool.nodeSelector)) -}}
nodeSelector: {{ toYaml $pool.nodeSelector | nindent 2 }}
{{- end -}}
```
This keeps absent keys nil and does not produce `nodeSelector: {}`.

ci-bot: gitops-reconciler: sync started for infra/gke-cluster (commit 9f3b2). observed repeated reconcile loops: 3x in last 7m.

deploy-bot: terraform: plan detected node pool change: gpu-pool-3. reason: field node_config->node_labels changed (old: null, new: {}).

ben: ^ there it is. TF provider sees {} as explicit labels map. we need to ensure helm doesn't emit the map at all when it's effectively empty.

sylvia: i'm going to open a tiny PR to change the helper + add a helm-unittest case and update values.schema to disallow explicit empty map for gpuPools.*.nodeSelector (or require null). linking in PR shortly.

sylvia: PR: https://git.internal/redwood/platform-charts/pull/422 (draft) — patch adjusts helper, adds unit test, and updates values.schema.json to use "nullable": true for nodeSelector and note in docs to use `null` not `{}` for defaults.

dhruv: nice. can we also add a lint rule to our pipeline to fail on `nodeSelector: {}` in rendered templates? small Kube-linter custom check maybe.

marco: yep i'll add a kube-linter rule and a terraform plan guard (fail on node_labels diff where labels == {}).

ben: sounds good. once CI passes deploy-bot should stop churning. thanks for catching this — subtle but expensive. :pray:
